            <ArticleTitle>Occluded stent in an extraluminal plane of the right coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>338-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jcct.2011.06.008</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary angiography demonstrated an occluded stent outside the lumen in the right coronary artery of a patient presenting with an acute coronary syndrome. Computed tomography confirmed the extraluminal location of the occluded stent. This finding is likely due to deployment of the stent in a dissection plane.</AbstractText>
